# Text is LF in every checkout, Windows included: the scripts run under bash, and the brand-asset lock
# (scripts/icons.ts) hashes text outputs byte for byte.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
# Every PR adds lines at the top of `## [Unreleased]`; git's built-in union driver keeps both sides
# instead of a conflict on every merge of main into a branch. Review the order after a merge.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
# Every branch lowers lines of the i18n baseline and none deletes one (a fixed file keeps its line at 0), so a local union
# merge (`git merge origin/main`, the merge train) keeps both versions of a lowered count and the reader takes the smaller
# (scripts/i18n/baseline.ts). GitHub's own merge ignores this attribute; no flow here relies on it. Two branches that
# lowered the same file leave the count above the real one: `i18n:check` says so, `bun run i18n:fix` repairs it.
i18n/hardcoded-baseline.jsonl merge=union
